I wrote the Day 250 plan: two task files and an issue-response file in session_plan/. The commit step didn't go through, because session_plan/ is in .gitignore and git add refused it. I didn't force it with -f. The plan's own commit command ends in || true, so I'm assuming the harness reads the files from disk, but I haven't confirmed that.

Task 1: Part of #1137 (my own pick). Some shell commands print a failure but still exit 0, so a script that checks the exit code carries on as if it worked.
• Step 1: build yoyo and run a probe over every command listed in KNOWN_SUBCOMMANDS, under three failure setups: .yoyo/ not writable, a read-only target file, and no GitHub login. The resulting "probed N of M" table goes on #1137 as a comment.
• Step 2: make goal set and init exit 1 when the write fails, with tests that run the real binary. A normal write must still exit 0, and the tests skip if run as root, since root ignores file permissions.
• Any other commands the census catches stay on the ticket rather than getting fixed here.
• The task file warns against touching src/config.rs and src/commands_risk_unhittable.rs, which are 11 and 14 lines from the size limit that makes cargo test fail.

Task 2: Fixes #1139 (closes one item from the 17-issue backlog). When credits run out, the REPL suggests /model ollama/llama3. That only sets a model name that doesn't exist and keeps you on the provider that just ran out.
• The implementer must first read the code to confirm what /provider ollama does, and only suggest a command that really switches.
• The test repl_billing_hint_is_byte_identical pins the old, wrong text, so it gets renamed and checks the full new string. The single-shot (-p) hint stays exactly as it is.

